# MotionSites — agent uses it, user vibes

The human does not configure tools. Do not ask them to Connect MCP, open
Settings, sign in to MotionSites, or connect Box.

“Boxes” means SSH servers. Use REA / `sailingsa/deploy/SSH_LIVE.md`. Never Box MCP.

When building or visually improving a website, landing, or hero, read
`.agents/skills/motionsites-web-builder/SKILL.md` and follow that workflow:

brief → 2–3 examples → real media → numbered spec → build → screenshot
loop until average 8 (nothing under 7). No adjective without a value.
SailingSA reuses design-system tokens and components. New marketing pages
may use the full cinematic skill. Never invent logos or asset URLs.

SailingSA live pages: keep the design system and locked header unless they
explicitly ask for a cinematic rebuild.

**Compact, modern, functional, mobile-portrait-first.** Kevin’s #1 design
complaint is agents making things large. SailingSA app chrome stays dense
(body ~14–16px, tight padding, small avatars, slim inputs, results lite
tables). MotionSites mega type (72–96px / 5–6× body) is only for a new
marketing hero the user asked for. Screenshot **390×844 first**, then ML,
then desktop. Clone the working sibling card — do not invent CSS. No large
blank areas, no giant full-width buttons, no overlay copy that hides the
photo on MP/ML, no stretched graphs, no overflow tables. Two identical
visual failures then diagnose; do not spawn another agent for the same
screenshot job.

Never again (from past chats): Cloud-over-Mac deploys; touch headers or
gold-header.css; thin-rewrite /dev1/; clobber live api.py with git; substring
logo matching; homepage fetching all roundup archives; prefilled login
fields; PUB_ public profiles; Lighthouse on a 502; invent results CSS;
Box MCP; MotionSites replacing the SailingSA layout; making app UI large
when it must be compact; ignoring mobile portrait.
